body:
As with others the headers now read &#34;datefolernametodo&#34;
I would like to see the completed tasks left in the day they were completed so I could go back and see when I completed it. As it is now I have to delete the reminder to get rid of it. 
Few issues but otherwise love the app

Também gosto do programa e uso ele com freqüência. Contudo, sinto a falta  das seguintes possibilidades:

1 - Alteração do som;
2 - No modo horizontal, a mudança dos meses exibidos deveria ser feita em modo slide, exibindo o meses anteriores ou próximos deslizando-se o dedo no mês que esta sendo mostrado;
3 - inclusão de mais de um alarme para o mesmo evento, como já é feito no calendário nativo.

One of the only features missing in this app is for the software to recognize dates and other scheduling information imputed using its voice-to-text feature and apply them to the task&#39;s additional information.  Ex: &#34;Call Emily Filbert. May 3rd at 10am. Flag important. Reminder at 9am.&#34;  

Hopefully a feature like this will become available in a later release.

I love having push notification for my to do list on my phone because I basically always have it with me when I&#39;m on the go.

Just started using this app but have many other todo&#39;s and this one is 5 Star so far...
2 months later;
I wish however after using it now for 2 months that their was &#34;I&#39;ll get to it one day&#34; file where I could store ie procrastinate on some items that have become much less urgent but should not be forgotten. Just a suggestion..

The app takes up to 4 secs to open when it hasnt been accesed longer period of times during the day, improving loading time would be useful;
Also UI can use an esthetic upgrade, I personally find the color scheme to dull.
Other than that good app, using it all the more each day

Habe schon viele Aufgabenverwaltungen getestet. Aber diese hier ist mir die allerliebste! Einfach und intuitiv, auch auf dem PC über chrome Plugin nutzbar. 
Was ich mir noch wünschen würde: 2 oder 3 wöchige Wiederholung und bei &#34;später&#34; noch 2 Tasten &#34;nächste Woche (Montag)&#34; und &#34;nächstes Wochenende (Samstag)&#34;
Sonst topp!

...Endlich das Richtige gefunden!
Any.Do ist super einfach zu bedienen, hat weder Werbung oder unnötigen Schnickschnack, sondern ist einfach intuitiv und easy. Ich bin absolut zufrieden und kann die App nur jedem, der seine Gedanken ordnen will, empfehlen. Die Sprach- und &#39;reminder&#39;- Funktion sind super! Da macht es auch nichts, dass die App auf englisch ist!
&#34;Download Tipp!&#34;

&#34;a wonderful job on all fronts in organizing my day and time. The UI is very crafty, simple, and elegant and I have used it more than the reminders app on Apples OS. Thanks to the developers for developing such a useful app for its users.&#34;

-previous review.

This premium monthly pricing for this app is an abomination on top of that yearly charge of 23.99 for some added color and unlimited any.do isn&#39;t worth. Worse update of the year...

When I first downloaded it, it said Today, Tomorrow, Upcoming and Someday.

When I updated it, it all changed.

The tab &#34;today&#34; changed into &#34; the name of this folder is today&#34;

Also the tab &#34;tomorrow&#34; changed into &#34;the name of this folder is tomorrow&#34;

Please: Any.do fix this quickly

Thanks,

Function is simple just like the design. I love using it. I have tried many list making apps. This one doesn&#39;t try to do too much but has a lot of features for power users. 
 Would love of they added location based features. &#34;Like remind me to buy AAAbateries when I am at target&#34;

I like that it also will show me my iCal events

I wish I could change the order of the tasks by dragging them, the way one moves apps around the home page on the iPhone. Also, if one&#39;s tasks haven&#39;t been completed by the end of the day, it would be cool to be notified and asked if they should be reclassified under &#34;tomorrow&#34; or &#34;someday.&#34; 
Finally, there should be an &#34;undo&#34; button in case you accidentally cross something off. 

Other than that, thanks for the app!

Such a clear design. Being a person who needs reminders, it does them so well. I love how it separates levels of importance. My favorite part is how it pops up around 10 every morning and says, &#34;Take a moment to plan your day.&#34; 
I always need that.
It&#39;s the perfect app.
